From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: brightnessManager: save the brightness of a panel without an EDID

Mutter has no vendor, product or serial for a panel without an EDID,
such as the DSI panels of these tablets, and returns null for them. A
GVariant string cannot be null, so every save threw "Argument string may
not be null" and no brightness was ever saved. Store a missing string
as an empty one; the connector still tells such panels apart.
Forwarded: no

--- a/js/misc/brightnessManager.js
+++ b/js/misc/brightnessManager.js
@@ -23,12 +23,15 @@
 
     static fromMonitor(logicalMonitor) {
         const monitor = logicalMonitor.get_monitors()[0];
+        // Mutter returns null for a string it does not have, such as the
+        // vendor, product and serial of a panel without an EDID (a DSI panel),
+        // and a GVariant string cannot be null.
         return new MonitorId({
-            vendor: monitor.get_vendor(),
-            product: monitor.get_product(),
-            serial: monitor.get_serial(),
+            vendor: monitor.get_vendor() ?? '',
+            product: monitor.get_product() ?? '',
+            serial: monitor.get_serial() ?? '',
             colorMode: '',
-            connector: monitor.get_connector(),
+            connector: monitor.get_connector() ?? '',
         });
     }
 
